= Ocean acidification — Simple =

'''Ocean acidification''' means the ocean's pH is gradually falling in many places as more carbon dioxide dissolves into seawater.

Extra dissolved carbon dioxide changes seawater chemistry. It increases substances associated with acidity and can reduce the availability of carbonate that some marine animals use to build shells or skeletons.

The ocean is still usually on the basic side of the pH scale; becoming **more acidic** does not necessarily mean its pH goes below 7.

The process is connected to the [[Carbon cycle|carbon cycle]] and the broader rise of atmospheric carbon dioxide.

